# Qwen3-Reranker-8B converted locally to GGUF by llama.cpp convert_hf_to_gguf.py.
# 'rank' pooling requires the classifier head the official converter preserves;
# a GGUF without it loads fine and returns meaningless scores, so the functional
# gate checks score ORDER, never merely that the endpoint answered.
SIDECAR_PORT=8082
SIDECAR_ALIAS=qwen3-reranker-8b
SIDECAR_MODEL=/home/typhoon/git/frankenstein-llm/models/reranker/Qwen3-Reranker-8B-Q6_K.gguf
SIDECAR_DEVICE=ROCm0,ROCm1,ROCm2
SIDECAR_NGL=all
SIDECAR_CTX=4096
SIDECAR_BATCH=1024
SIDECAR_UBATCH=1024
# Placement: one card. 3,6,2 was the pre-2026-09-06 catalog default and gave the
# throttling V620 the majority of the layers of a model that fits on a single
# 6900 XT. llama-models.ini stopped using it in f2576ac; this file was not
# updated with it. Layer split is pipelined, so every token crossed two extra
# devices for no capacity reason. Measured on kernel 7.2.3-273-tkg-eevdf-llvm,
# pp512/tg128, r=3, native llama-bench: 34.72 -> 65.31 tok/s decode (+88.1%),
# 1233.73 -> 1425.14 tok/s prefill (+15.5%). Reranking never decodes, so the
# prefill figure is the one that describes this service.
SIDECAR_EXTRA_ARGS=--reranking --pooling rank --flash-attn off --cache-type-v f16 --tensor-split 1,0,0
